# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Knowledge vault .gitignore  — policy: git tracks NOTES ONLY
# (markdown notes, READMEs, SRS deck, journals, small text).
# Code repos, course material, binaries, media and anything
# work-related or secret stay on disk but are never committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. Work / employer material (Gain Insights) — sensitive, never commit
/work/

# 2. Bulky learning material: whole repos, courses, samples, datasets, media
technical/**/courses/**
# ...but keep the docs I write for Udemy courses (README, roadmap, resources, skipped list)
!technical/**/courses/udemy-*/
!technical/**/courses/udemy-*/*.md
technical/**/projects/
technical/**/examples/
technical/**/datasets/
technical/**/media/
softskills/**/courses/
softskills/**/media/

# 3. Secrets anywhere
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*
credentials*.json

# 4. Binary documents (kept on disk, not in git)
*.pdf
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.qvf
*.qvd
*.pbix

# 5. Archives, media, images, models
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.gz
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.avi
*.mp3
*.wav
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.bin
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.pkl
*.h5

# 6. Dependencies, envs, caches, build output
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.idea/
.next/
build/
dist/
*.log
logs/

# 7. OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
__MACOSX/
*.tmp
~$*

# 8. Vault tooling
_resume-pack.md
.inbox/

# 9. Local-only audit / tenant-specific links (mention work paths or tenant IDs)
_meta/restructure-log.tsv
technical/data-ai/anomaly-detection/docs/fabric-kql-mvad-onelake-links.txt
